{
  "requirement": "List project-relative file paths in the [selected scope](search.md#choosing-a-source-scope).\nOmitting `prefix` lists all visible project files. If more paths remain, follow `next` as shown in\n[Continuing a paged result](#continuing-a-paged-result).",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.list_sources.behavior`. I found no gaps.\n\n**Obligations**\n1. List project-relative file paths in the selected scope. The scope is a directory prefix, a single-file prefix or the whole project, as `search.md#choosing-a-source-scope` describes.\n2. Omitting `prefix` lists all visible project files. Visible means files that ignore rules don't exclude.\n3. If more paths remain, the result carries `next`, and following it continues the listing.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Prefix omitted and paging:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[listing_continuations_return_complete_paths_from_the_original_listing]` creates 200 long file names and calls `list_sources` with `{}`.\n  - It asserts that `next` is present, then follows `get_next_page` until `next` is absent.\n  - It asserts that the concatenated paths equal the full expected list, in order and as complete project-relative paths. The listing is not affected by a file added after the first page.\n- **Prefix naming a file:** `fn[fixed_tools_deliver_domain_contents_with_mandatory_snapshot_dependencies]` lists with `prefix: \"source.txt\"`. It asserts the exact result `{\"files\":[\"source.txt\"]}`, which covers the single-file scope and the relative-path form.\n- **Prefix naming a directory, with ignore rules:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_agent_uses_attached_project_tools_in_both_configuration_orders]` lists with `prefix: \"visible\"`.\n  - The directory holds a `.gitignore`d file, and a different project root also has a `visible/` directory.\n  - It asserts that the listing is exactly `[\"visible/selected.txt\"]`, which shows prefix scoping and ignored-file exclusion. Only the selected project's files appear. This runs in both configuration orders.\n- **Argument forwarding:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results]` calls `list_sources` with no prefix and with `\"src/\"`. It asserts that the provider receives scope prefixes `\"\"` and `\"src/\"`, and that the output is `{\"files\":[...]}`.\n- **Discovery and its pages:** `fn[source_discovery_and_its_pages_do_not_register_reads]` runs `list_sources` with `{}` and follows its pages.\n- **Provider-level scope and visibility:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository]` checks `Sources::list` with `SourceScope::all()`, which equals the default scope.\n  - It asserts that ignored files, including a Git-tracked ignored file, are excluded. Nested exceptions and dotfiles are included.\n  - Listing under an ignored file or directory returns an empty result.\n  - It runs with and without a Git repository.\n\n**Conclusion**\nEvery clause of the subject (scope selection, the default of all visible files, and `next` continuation) has a test with concrete assertions. Each test carries a `{test}` reference to the subject.",
  "references": "9b598dbede71c61e2c43c9e0f863580c991f6cfd534e580bd5593f70e3d26cfc",
